        "title": "Strong growth, ambitious cloud outlook",
        "html": "<style>body{margin:0;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:#172b42;background:#f4f7fb}*{box-sizing:border-box}.wrap{padding:40px}.eyebrow{font-size:15px;letter-spacing:2px;color:#536982}.panel{background:white;border:1px solid #dce4ed;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;height:100%}h1{font-size:38px;font-weight:700;margin:12px 0}h2{font-size:23px;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:16px}p{font-size:18px;line-height:1.45}.metric{font-size:32px;font-weight:700;color:#145c89}.small-label{font-size:16px;color:#536982}.table{font-size:18px}.table td,.table th{padding:10px 0}.risk{background:#fff3e8;border-left:5px solid #c77a31;padding:20px;border-radius:8px}footer{font-size:15px;color:#536982;margin-top:22px}</style><div class='wrap'><div class='eyebrow'>MICROSOFT · FY27 Q1 EARNINGS OUTLOOK</div><h1>Strong actual growth. Ambitious guidance.</h1><p>Delivery depends on engineering efficiency, capacity timing, token economics and demand conversion—not demand alone.</p><div class='row g-4 mt-2'><div class='col-6'><div class='panel'><h2>Reported · September 30 quarter</h2><div class='row'><div class='col-6'><div class='metric'>$92.3B</div><div class='small-label'>Revenue · +19% YoY</div></div><div class='col-6'><div class='metric'>48%</div><div class='small-label'>Azure growth</div></div></div><table class='table mt-3 mb-0'><tbody><tr><td>Operating income / margin</td><td>$45.9B / 50%</td></tr><tr><td>Microsoft Cloud</td><td>$63.9B · +30%</td></tr><tr><td>Commercial RPO</td><td>$677B · +73%</td></tr><tr><td>Capex</td><td>$45.2B</td></tr><tr><td>Operating / free cash flow</td><td>$58B / $18.6B</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class='col-6'><div class='panel'><h2>Expected · December quarter</h2><div class='row'><div class='col-6'><div class='metric'>$96–97.1B</div><div class='small-label'>Revenue · +18–19%</div></div><div class='col-6'><div class='metric'>49–50%</div><div class='small-label'>Azure · constant currency</div></div></div><table class='table mt-3 mb-0'><tbody><tr><td>Cloud gross margin</td><td>About 65%</td></tr><tr><td>Company operating margin</td><td>Slightly lower YoY</td></tr><tr><td>Q2 capex</td><td>Above $50B</td></tr><tr><td>Calendar-year capex</td><td>About $170B</td></tr><tr><td>FY2027 free cash flow</td><td>Expected positive</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div><div class='row g-4 mt-1'><div class='col-7'><div class='panel'><h2>Q&A · How returns are supported</h2><p><b>Nadella:</b> one fungible capacity pool supports Azure and Fabric, Foundry and Copilot through efficiency, demand allocation and stack reinforcement.</p><p class='mb-0'><b>Hood:</b> application-to-memory efficiencies helped allocate more capacity to Foundry in the reported quarter. Further engineering progress is still required.</p></div></div><div class='col-5'><div class='risk'><h2>Execution dependencies &amp; risks</h2><p>Engineering efficiency · Capacity timing · Token economics · Demand conversion</p><p class='mb-0'>Demand exceeds supply. Token pricing and delayed capacity remain uncertain; some third-party GPU capacity shifted to the second half.</p></div></div></div><footer>Lecture-stated source: October 28, 2026 investor call. Guidance reflects management expectations as of that date, not completed results.</footer></div>"
      }
